    "inspectNotes": "Bead b3-weight-fn BLOCKED: commit d813b8b4 does not implement computeSubstrateBugWeight(criteria, stats) at all. The diff only adds optional weight/weightReason fields to the FlywheelSuggestion interface/schema in packages/contracts/src/flywheel.ts:180-190 — no status-multiplier logic, no normalizedDistance calculation, no compound-value field reading (medianMs/p95Ms), no insufficient_data short-circuit, and no reason-string generation exist anywhere in this commit. None of AC1-AC5 can be evaluated because the function under review is absent. This is the same d813b8b4 diff already submitted (and blocked) against bead b2-parse-criteria moments ago — it looks like the wrong commit is being routed to review requests, or the actual b3-weight-fn implementation commit has not landed yet. Required fix: identify and deliver the commit that actually adds computeSubstrateBugWeight, implementing per-criterion status multiplier (red=1.6x per AC1 example: 3*(1+0.6)), a status floor that dominates over raw normalized drift for red vs green (AC2), safe reading of a configured valueField from compound values with graceful fallback to normalizedDistance 0 + floor when the field is absent (AC3), a weight-0 + insufficient-telemetry-reason short circuit when all criteria are insufficient_data (AC4), and a reason string naming the highest-contributing criterion by label/status/value-vs-target (AC5).",
